$ whycant -u alice read /home/alice/notes.txt

✗ alice (uid 1000) cannot read /home/alice/notes.txt

  /                       drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /home                   drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /home/alice             drwxr-xr-x  alice:alice  ✓ traverse
  /home/alice/notes.txt   ----r--rwx  alice:alice  ✗ read   ← blocked here

Why
  alice owns /home/alice/notes.txt, so only the owner permissions apply: ---.
  Reading a file needs r.
  The group (r--) and other (rwx) permissions would allow it, but they never
  apply to the owner: owner bits are used on their own.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Give the owner (alice) the missing r permission:
       chmod u+r /home/alice/notes.txt
